# Skill: Self-review before merge request

Use this skill to run through a quick self-review before opening or finalizing a merge request.

## Code quality

- [ ] Follows project style guide (Documentation/Development/style/readme.md and language-specific guides).
- [ ] No commented-out code; no unnecessary debug logging.
- [ ] Meaningful names; no magic numbers/strings without constants.
- [ ] Functions/methods small and focused; single responsibility.

## Tests and checks

- [ ] Unit tests added or updated for new/changed behavior.
- [ ] Backend: `mvn checkstyle:check test` passes.
- [ ] Frontend: `gulp eslint test` (or equivalent) passes.
- [ ] No sensitive data (passwords, tokens, keys) in code or commits.

## Security and errors

- [ ] User input validated/sanitized; parameterized queries (no string concatenation for SQL).
- [ ] Errors handled gracefully; user-facing messages are clear, no raw stack traces.
- [ ] Appropriate log levels; no logging of sensitive data.

## Version control and docs

- [ ] Branch name follows convention: `username/version/-XXXX_short_description` (see @contributing).
- [ ] Commit messages in imperative mood; JIRA reference when applicable.
- [ ] Documentation updated where behavior or API changed (see @update-documentation).

## Merge request

- [ ] Description explains what and why; links JIRA if applicable.
- [ ] Reviewers assigned; ready for human review.

Reference: .cursor/rules/general.mdc, .cursor/rules/contributing.mdc.
